==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sea King Daliasan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''God-Emperor Daliasan''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Daliasan has good health, high damage (especially with [[Savage Blow]]), and long standing range. Use Daliasan as you would [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Radiant Aphrodite]], as it is an amazing backliner to snipe enemies that otherwise would be protected. The ability to [[Slow]] Angel and Floating enemies keeps them from pushing forward, improving its attacks and overall support for other units. [[Colossus Slayer]] greatly enhances its niche in [[Gauntlet]]s, especially [[Mega Menace]] and [[Divine Archangel Strikes]] being Floating- and Angel- focused respectively.

The presence of a blind spot enforces the need to protect Daliasan. Use [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] or similar to constantly protect Daliasan against close-ranged enemies that can enter its blind spot. Finally, it is also worth noting that this unit is also part of a very efficient [[Cat Combo]]: [[Dragon Aquarium (Combo)|Dragon Aquarium]], which gives a 15% percent speed boost to all your units for the cost of only two slots! Moreover, if you have the units, this can be paired with the [[Enter The Ninja (Combo)|Enter The Ninja]] Cat Combo, giving a whopping 30% boost.

==='''True Form'''===
True Form increases Daliasan's chance to perform a Savage Blow by 10%, giving a substantial effective 18.3% DPS increase (+811 DPS at Lv.30), in addition to a more consistent chance. Naturally, this directly bolsters Daliasan's usage from an already good Super-Backliner to a great one.

The increased HP serves to improve Daliasan's already great flexibility & survivability with its 7 knockback count. Alone finding itself more worthwhile than Radiant Aphrodite's True Form; with Daliasan's lower standing range, this stat increase is a nice bonus to its kit.

Daliasan receives a rather substantial speed increase, nearly doubling its movement speed from 5 to 8. Daliasan can now more easily reach the front line and provide better pushing power to your army too. Although, while a large boost percentage-wise, in practice, Daliasan is still rather slow.

Finally, a very important thing to note is Daliasan's cheap True Form evolve materials, being only 3 [[Catfruit|Green Catfruit]], 3 Yellow Catfruit, and 4 Epic Catfruit. True forming an Uber is usually much more expensive, which makes unlocking Daliasan's True Form an easy task.

Overall, this True Form is worth your Catfruit, improving Daliasan's utility and capabilities in the ways that matter most, solidifying it as a mainstay Generalist Super-Backliner & Sniper.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Survive]]''' is some real eye candy here, and to its credit, it's an extremely valuable ability on a superbackliner like Daliasan. Its recharge rate is abysmally long, so this is a means to solidify its longevity by ensuring an additional opportunity to reposition regardless of the situation at hand.

'''[[Immune to Waves]]''' has a lot more generalist application than it does specialist. Daliasan's endurance is practically non-existent, so it was previously very prone to getting juggled to death by Wave Attacks of any kind. This Talent makes it much more reliable overall, excelling in confrontations against a plethora of non-targets without the need for Wave Shields. Notably, in [[Divine Archangel Strikes/Blessing Lv.1~20|Blessing Lv.11~20]], it now entirely counters the stage and its supports.

'''[[Immune to Weaken]]''' is significantly less noteworthy, being situationally good against [[Calamary]], [[Cli-One]], and [[Great Angel Chibinel]], with not much use elsewhere. You could hypothetically use Daliasan against [[E-792]], but it's outranged by the Cyclone's effective Long Distance reach, which leads to this leviathan getting juggled to death if the Cyclone's constantly attacking. None of these scenarios warrant this Talent, but the option is there for players looking for a counter.

Finally, '''Attack buff''' is never a bad idea, but invest into Daliasan with [[Catseye]]s before seriously considering it. '''HP Buff''' doesn't fix its poor endurance, but can allow it to survive for an additional reposition depending on the situation. It's still generally not worth the NP for such a minute upgrade.

