==Trivia==
*The name Daliasan appears to be a portmanteau of ''[[wikipedia:Darius (series)|Darius]]'', a shoot 'em up video game series which features many fish-like enemies, and ''[[wikipedia:Leviathan|Leviathan]]'', a sea monster mentioned in the Bible. It seems to have been mistranslated, as while ダライアサン can be read as "Daliasan", an equally valid reading is "Dariathan", which makes both of the references more apparent.
**Daliasan's design is somewhat reminiscent of [[wikia:darius:King Fossil|King Fossil]], the most iconic boss of the ''Darius'' series, while its attack animation is likely a reference to the [[wikia:darius:Dimension Diver|Dimension Diver]] from ''[[wikia:darius:G-Darius|G-Darius]]''.
**Sea King Daliasan is the only unit in the game to have a [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]] on either side of its body, unlike other units that have [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Normal Cat]]/[[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]]. Since Daliasan has horns and Brainwashed Cat is the allied counterpart of [[Wicked Cat (Enemy)|Wicked Cat]], an [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]], this may be a reference to how Leviathan has both been identified with the Devil and considered one of the Princes of Hell.
***In this regard, [[Jumbo Jones]] can be seen as a foil to Daliasan, an [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel]] Colossus Slayer. Daliasan exhibits demonic traits, but is on the player's side, whereas Jumbo Jones is an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]], perhaps representing the interpretation of Leviathan as simply another of God's creations, but is on the enemies' side. Both also have Long Distance and Slow abilities.

